   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the general municipal law, in relation to permitting the\nJohnson City school district to create an insurance reserve fund",
    "basePrintNo": "S8513",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8513-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §6-n, Gen Muni L",
    "lawSection": "General Municipal Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8513\n\nSPONSOR: WEBB\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the general municipal law, in relation to permitting the\nJohnson City school district to create an insurance reserve fund\n\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAN ACT to amend the General Municipal Law, in relation to permitting the\nJohnson City School District to create an insurance reserve fund\n\n \nPURPOSE OR THE BILL:\n\nThis bill allows the Johnson City School District to establish an insur-\nance reserve fund for the purpose of making payments related to health-\nrelated claims.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. Amends section 6-n of the General Municipal Law to add the\nJohnson City School District to the list of school districts within the\nstate authorized to establish an insurance reserve fund.\n\nSection 2. Establishes the effective date\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nIn an effort to control the rising costs associated with insurance\npremiums, many school districts are transitioning to a self-insured\nhealth insurance model to provide coverage for their faculty and staff.\nThe Johnson City School District has elected to provide coverage through\nsuch a plan effective January 1, 2026.\n\nAlthough the overall cost associated with a self-insured plan is lower\nthan a traditional health plan, there are greater cost fluctuations\nresulting from the unpredictability of resulting health claims. With\nschool districts being prohibited from retaining more than four percent\nof their budget in an unappropriated fund balance or reserve fund, this\nsignificantly limits the Johnson City School District's ability to\nprepare for the variable expenses of the self-insured plan.\n\nThis bill would allow the school district to create an insurance reserve\nand avoid fiscal hardship due to the variability of these types of claim\nand lower their overall budgetary expenses.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE. HISTORY:\n\nNew bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATION:\n\nNone to the State\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
    "multiSponsors": {
