    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8513A\n\nSPONSOR: WEBB\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the general municipal law, in relation to permitting the\nJohnson City central school district to create an insurance reserve fund\n\n \nPURPOSE OF THE BILL:\n\nThis bill allows the Johnson City Central School District to establish\nan insurance reserve fund for the purpose of making payments related to\nhealth-related claims.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. Amends section 6-n of the General Municipal Law to add the\nJohnson City Central School District to the list of school districts\nwithin the state authorized to establish an insurance reserve fund.\n\nSection 2. Establishes the effective date\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nIn an effort to control the rising costs associated with insurance\npremiums, many school districts are transitioning to a self-insured\nhealth insurance model to provide coverage for their faculty and staff.\nThe Johnson City Central School District has elected to provide coverage\nthrough such a plan effective January 1, 2026.\n\nAlthough the overall cost associated with a self-insured plan is lower\nthan a traditional health plan, there are greater cost fluctuations\nresulting from the unpredictability of resulting health claims. With\nschool districts being prohibited from retaining more than four percent\nof their budget in an unappropriated fund balance or reserve fund, this\nsignificantly limits the Johnson City School District's ability to\nprepare for the variable expenses of the self-insured plan.\n\nThis bill would allow the school district to create an insurance reserve\nand avoid fiscal hardship due to the variability of these types of\nclaims and lower, their overall budgetary expenses.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATION:\n\nNone to the State\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
